<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE task PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Task//EN" "task.dtd">
<!-- Move between workspaces, shared by the Android phone and tablet, iPhone, iPad and Mac (issue 196, issue 200).
     Walked on 17 November 2026: on each, Open another workspace on Home and Workspaces itself list a card for
     each tree, the tree in use first and marked Active. Open on another card goes straight to that tree's Home,
     with no message. The tablet, iPad and Mac show the cards side by side. On the Mac the screen was locked, so
     it was read through the app's own tree, not seen. -->
<task id="move-between-workspaces" xml:lang="en-GB">
  <title>Move between workspaces</title>
  <shortdesc>Open another of your trees, and see which one is in use now.</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <critdates>
      <created date="2026-11-17"/>
    </critdates>
    <metadata>
      <audience type="user" experiencelevel="novice"/>
      <category>How-to</category>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>switch tree</keyword>
        <keyword>open another tree</keyword>
        <keyword>change tree</keyword>
      </keywords>
    </metadata>
    <resourceid appname="ufti" appid="workspaces.switch"/>
  </prolog>
  <taskbody>
    <context>
      <p>You can keep more than one tree. Each one is a <term keyref="term-workspace">workspace</term>, and each has a card on <uicontrol keyref="ui-workspaces"/>. Only one tree is in use at a time.</p>
    </context>
    <steps>
      <step>
        <cmd>On <uicontrol keyref="ui-home"/>, choose <uicontrol keyref="ui-open-another-workspace"/>.</cmd>
        <info>
          <p><ph platform="AndroidPhone iPhone iPad MacCatalyst">Or choose <uicontrol keyref="ui-more"/>, then <uicontrol keyref="ui-workspaces"/>.</ph><ph platform="AndroidTablet">Or choose <uicontrol keyref="ui-workspaces"/> in the list on the left.</ph></p>
        </info>
        <stepresult>
          <p>Each tree has a card. The card of the tree in use comes first, with a dark border, and is marked <uicontrol keyref="ui-active"/>.<ph platform="AndroidTablet iPad MacCatalyst"> The cards sit side by side.</ph></p>
          <fig>
            <image keyref="img-workspaces"/>
          </fig>
        </stepresult>
      </step>
      <step>
        <cmd>Choose <uicontrol keyref="ui-open"/> on the card of the tree you want.</cmd>
        <stepresult>
          <p><uicontrol keyref="ui-home"/> opens for that tree at once. Its name is at the top, and its card is now marked <uicontrol keyref="ui-active"/>.</p>
        </stepresult>
      </step>
    </steps>
    <result>
      <p>Everything you see now is from the tree you chose. Your changes to the other tree were saved as you made them, so nothing is lost when you move.</p>
      <p>To see which file a tree is, choose <uicontrol keyref="ui-show-details"/> on its card. The button then reads <uicontrol keyref="ui-hide-details"/>.</p>
    </result>
    <postreq>
      <p>Next: <xref keyref="where-your-trees-are-saved"/>.</p>
    </postreq>
  </taskbody>
</task>
